FILED s536a (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-08) from #135 (Role-Tiny stub.t rows 2 / 4, role-tiny-with.t row 5).  PRE-EXISTING on main 06a4b8ba (code sha).

REPRODUCER (scratch/s536a/p/135-7.pl in the s536a worktree):

    package CW;
    sub stubsub;
    sub later { 1 }
    package main;
    no strict 'refs';
    print "keys: ", join(" ", sort grep !/::$/, keys %{"CW::"}), "\n";
    print "exists stub: ", (exists &CW::stubsub ? 1 : 0), " defined: ", (defined &CW::stubsub ? 1 : 0), "\n";
    *{"D::copy"} = \&CW::stubsub;
    print "D exists: ", (exists &D::copy ? 1 : 0), " defined: ", (defined &D::copy ? 1 : 0), "\n";
    my $code = \&{"CW::stubsub"};
    *{"E::copy2"} = $code;
    print "E exists: ", (exists &E::copy2 ? 1 : 0), " defined: ", (defined &E::copy2 ? 1 : 0), "\n";

perl 5.40.3: `keys: later stubsub` / `exists stub: 1 defined: 0` / `D exists: 1 defined: 0` / `E exists: 1 defined: 0`.
PCL: `keys: later` (the stub is missing) / `exists stub: 1 defined: 0` / `D exists: 1 defined: 1` / `E exists: 1 defined: 1`.

TWO halves, one fact -- a perl forward declaration `sub NAME;` IS a stash entry (a CV with no body):
(a) THE VIEW: p-stash skips every :stub on purpose (its comment: Moo::Role's make_role must not see subs PCL only PRE-declares).  But PCL emits two kinds of stub -- `(p-declare-sub pl-NAME)` for the file's own bodyless `sub NAME;` (perl's stub) and `(p-declare-sub pl-NAME :body)` for its pre-declaration of a sub the file DEFINES later -- and both set :stub, so the view cannot tell them apart.  Role::Tiny's _all_subs (`grep exists &{...}, keys %$stash`) therefore misses a class's own stub (stub.t row 2: the role's sub composes over it) and a role's stub (stub.t row 4, role-tiny-with.t row 5: never composed).  Complication: Parser2's cross-section re-emission (`(pcl:p-declare-sub Pkg::pl-NAME)`, Parser2.pm ~2797) emits the nil arm for :body names too.
(b) THE COPY: `*X = \&stub` installs the trampoline p-backslash-sub hands out with *p-declared-subs* :defined (%p-glob-install-code), so `defined &X` is true where perl's copied stub CV is not defined.

FIX SHAPE (not built; an emission change, gen bump): a `:forward` arm of p-declare-sub for the file's OWN bodyless declaration (Parser.pm ~11725 and Parser2.pm ~10990; the cross-section regex preserves it) recorded in a set the stash view reads beside %p-sub-has-body-p; %p-glob-install-code installs :stub (not :defined) when FN is a lazy-coderef trampoline whose target has no body (*p-lazy-coderef-target*).  BAR: the reproducer; Role-Tiny stub.t 4/4 and role-tiny-with.t 6/6 one-file; Pl/t guard rows; corpus-diff = every file with a bodyless `sub NAME;`.
ROWS: Role-Tiny-2.002004-0 stub.t 2 and 4, role-tiny-with.t 5 (re-keyed from #135 by s536a).


=== DONE (s536b) ===
FIXED (s536b, Opus 5.5, 2026-11-08; commits 30b95ac1 + 4cf10dc4, generation v2-12200).  Both halves:
(a) THE VIEW -- a new `:forward` arm of p-declare-sub, emitted for the file's OWN bodyless `sub NAME;` by the ONE spelling Pl::Parser::declare_sub_form (v1's named-sub path, Parser2's top-level route and _lower_named_sub_stmt, which used to spell its own `['p-declare-sub', NAME]`); it is the nil arm plus a record in `*p-forward-subs*`.  p-stash lists a symbol that has a body OR is a live forward declaration; the nil arm (Parser2's cross-section call stubs -- its regex now also matches `:forward` lines) and the `:body` pre-declaration of a later-defined sub stay hidden (the Moo::Role invariant of decl-ordering-02.t).
(b) THE COPY -- NOT at the install (s536a's %p-glob-install-code is in flight on that code): `defined &NAME` reads the CODE slot -- a late-bound ref to a stub (p-backslash-sub's trampoline / fallback, *p-lazy-coderef-target*) whose target has no body is NOT defined.  ONE predicate `%p-lazy-stub-p`, shared with p-coderef-defined-p (`defined &$code`).  The late binding is kept: after the target gets a body, `D::copy()` runs it and `defined &D::copy` is true (perl's shared CV).
Probe scratch/s536b/p/s1.pl: tree = perl on every line (keys, exists / defined of the stub, of `*D::copy = \&stub`, of `*E::copy2 = $code`, the copy's call dies naming the target, the late definition).  Guard: Pl/t/decl-ordering-02.t row 32 (perl differential), inverse-verified on 0affbe86; Pl/t/parser2-01.t's shape row now asserts `(p-declare-sub pl-t1 :forward)` (strengthened, the stale-guard rule).
